---
name: plan-hardening-finding-bead
version: 1.0.0
description: One reviewer finding from a plan-hardening review step (2, 4 or 6) as a bead, a child of the phase root, discovered from that step's bead. The runner files one per entry in the reviewer's `findings` and `minor_wording` (for ceremony-qa, `data.findings`). The planner closes it in the next correction step with its ruling as the reason; it blocks the next review step's bead. Render strictly, then `jq -c .` into the import JSONL.
format: json
required_variables:
  - id
  - root
  - phase
  - step_bead
  - reviewer
  - finding_ref
  - severity
  - category
  - issue
  - correction
defaults:
  target_refs: []
---
{% set sev = severity | lower %}{% if sev not in ["blocking", "important", "minor"] %}ERROR: severity must be blocking, important or minor, got {{ severity }}
{% endif %}{
  "id": {{ id | tojson }},
  "title": {{ ("phase-" ~ phase ~ " plan " ~ sev ~ ": " ~ finding_ref ~ " " ~ category) | tojson }},
  "issue_type": "bug",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": {{ {"blocking": 1, "important": 2, "minor": 4}[sev] }},
  "description": {{ (issue ~ "\n\n## Correction\n" ~ correction ~ "\n\n## Targets\n" ~ (target_refs | join("\n"))) | tojson }},
  "design": {{ correction | tojson }},
  "labels": {{ ["phase-" ~ phase, "stage:plan-finding", "severity:" ~ sev] | tojson }},
  "dependencies": [
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ root | tojson }}, "type": "parent-child"},
    {"issue_id": {{ id | tojson }}, "depends_on_id": {{ step_bead | tojson }}, "type": "discovered-from"}
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "reviewer": {{ reviewer | tojson }},
    "finding_ref": {{ finding_ref | tojson }},
    "severity": {{ sev | tojson }},
    "category": {{ category | tojson }},
    "target_refs": {{ target_refs | tojson }}
  }
}
